3. PAIRWISE INTERACTIONS DETECTED (2):
   [CONTRAINDICATED] Warfarin ⟷ Amiodarone
       Mechanism:  Pharmacokinetic (CYP2C9/CYP3A4 Inhibition) — Amiodarone potently inhibits CYP2C9 and CYP3A4, the principal clearance pathways of active S-warfarin and R-warfarin. This leads to marked accumulation of warfarin.
       Effect:     Dramatically elevated INR, severe life-threatening internal hemorrhage, and gastrointestinal/intracranial bleeding.
       Management: Avoid combination if possible. If concomitant use is clinically mandatory, empirically reduce warfarin maintenance dose by 33% to 50% upon starting amiodarone and monitor INR every 48-72 hours until stable.
