   [SEVERE] Warfarin ⟷ Aspirin
       Mechanism:  Pharmacodynamic (Additive Antithrombotic / Mucosal Erosion) — Aspirin causes irreversible platelet COX-1 inhibition and direct gastric mucosal barrier breakdown, while warfarin inhibits clotting factor synthesis.
       Effect:     Exponential 3-fold to 5-fold surge in major gastrointestinal bleeding and intracranial hemorrhage.
       Management: Concomitant therapy should be reserved strictly for clear mechanical valve or recent ACS indications. Add a gastroprotective proton pump inhibitor (e.g., Pantoprazole) and monitor hemoglobin/hematocrit.
       Citations:  J Am Coll Cardiol 2018; 71(13):1454-1466

