2. SAFETY DETERMINATION: [CONTRAINDICATED] (Evaluated in 0.32 ms)

3. PAIRWISE INTERACTIONS DETECTED (2):
   [SEVERE] Sertraline ⟷ Tramadol
       Mechanism:  Pharmacodynamic (Additive Serotonergic Reuptake Blockade) — Sertraline blocks 5-HT reuptake, while Tramadol inhibits serotonin and norepinephrine reuptake and mildly stimulates 5-HT release.
       Effect:     Precipitation of Serotonin Syndrome: autonomic instability, neuromuscular hyperreflexia, clonus, hyperthermia, and seizures.
       Management: Avoid co-administration. If analgesia is required, use non-serotonergic analgesics (e.g. Acetaminophen, short-term NSAID if non-contraindicated).
       Citations:  Am J Psychiatry 2007; 164(9):1339-1346
   [CONTRAINDICATED] Sertraline ⟷ Linezolid
       Mechanism:  Pharmacodynamic (MAO-A Inhibition + SSRI Storm) — Linezolid has non-selective, reversible monoamine oxidase (MAO) inhibitory activity. Combining it with an SSRI blocks both 5-HT breakdown and reuptake.
       Effect:     Severe, potentially fatal Serotonin Syndrome with hyperthermia, rhabdomyolysis, disseminated intravascular coagulation, and death.
       Management: CONTRAINDICATED. Linezolid must not be administered to patients receiving SSRIs unless emergency situation with close ICU monitoring and immediate discontinuation of SSRI.
       Citations:  FDA Safety Announcement 2011, Clin Infect Dis 2006; 42(11):1578-1583

4. CUMULATIVE MULTI-DRUG TOXICITY INDICES:
